# SRI-pinned vendored assets whose committed integrity= hash is the LF-bytes
# hash: mark them `binary` so git never rewrites line endings on any platform.
# The docker-compose bind mount serves the working-copy bytes straight to the
# browser, which verifies them against the integrity= attribute in
# src/aia/index.html, so the served bytes must equal the committed blob.
#
# (marked.min.js / dompurify.min.js are deliberately NOT listed here — their
# committed hashes match a CRLF working copy on this autocrlf=true repo;
# normalising those two + adding a CI guard is a tracked follow-up.)
src/aia/scripts/diff-match-patch.js  binary
src/aia/css/katex.min.css            binary
